---
title: CI job graph
---
%% Source of truth: .github/workflows/ci.yml — `needs:` and `if:` on each job.
flowchart LR
    accTitle: What CI runs on a push, and what decides whether each job runs
    accDescr: A paths-filter job runs first and emits five booleans; every other job except pre-commit gates on one of them, so a docs-only change skips the Python matrix entirely. The jobs then run flat and in parallel — there is no second tier, so no job waits on another's result. Two of them exist specifically to turn a silent skip into a failure: conformance sets FELIX_CONFORMANCE_REQUIRE_POSTGRES so a missing database fails instead of skipping an arm, and test sets FELIX_REQUIRE_OPTIONAL_EXTRAS so a missing extra fails instead of quietly collecting nothing.

    push([push or pull_request]) --> changes

    changes{"changes<br/>dorny/paths-filter"} -->|"python"| lint["lint<br/>ruff check + format"]
    changes -->|"python"| typecheck["typecheck<br/>ty check packages apps"]
    changes -->|"python"| test["test<br/>pytest, all extras"]
    changes -->|"python"| conf["conformance<br/>store + provider contracts"]
    changes -->|"python"| evaljob["eval<br/>mock fixture, no model calls"]
    changes -->|"python"| lean["lean<br/>no-extras install, import every module"]
    changes -->|"toolkit"| toolkit["toolkit<br/>validate .claude hooks and skills"]
    changes -->|"helm"| helm["helm<br/>lint + topology test"]
    changes -->|"docker"| docker["docker<br/>compose config, every overlay"]
    changes -.->|"scalar, gates one step inside lint"| lint

    push -->|"ungated, runs on every push"| pre["pre-commit"]

    class changes focal
    class test focal
    class push external
    class lint,typecheck,conf,evaljob,lean,toolkit,helm,docker,pre primary

    classDef focal    fill:#dbeaf5,stroke:#0072B2,stroke-width:2px,color:#062033
    classDef primary  fill:#f4f6f9,stroke:#5a6272,stroke-width:1px,color:#10203a
    classDef external fill:#ffffff,stroke:#767676,stroke-width:1px,stroke-dasharray:4 3,color:#3b414d
